Package: facomplex
Title: Methods for Assessing Factor Complexity and Simplicity in Factor Analysis Solutions
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Merino-Soto", "Cesar A.", 
           email = "sikayax@yahoo.com.ar", 
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Dominguez-Lara", "Sergio", 
           email = "sdominguezmpcs@gmail.com", 
           role = c("ctb"))
    )
Description: Provides methods for examining factorial complexity and simplicity in multidimensional scales, as well as in unidimensional scales when compared, in exploratory and ESEM factor analysis (EFA) results. The package implements coefficients derived from the work of Kaiser, Hofmann, Flemings, Bentler, and Lorenzo-Seva. The sums of the squares of the factorial loads (target and non-target loadings) can be estimated for descriptive purposes. Point estimates and confidence intervals are also obtained using bootstrap simulation.
